<title>UK: Russian oil port Novorossiisk reopens.</title>
<headline>Russian oil port Novorossiisk reopens.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-02-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Russian oil export terminal of Novorossiisk was open to tankers on Friday after being closed due to bad weather, a shipping source said.</p>
<p>The source said the 650,000 barrel per day port reopened at 0900 local time.</p>
<p>Latvia's oil export port of Ventspils was also open, as were the Ukraine's Black Sea port of Odessa and the Russian oil export terminal at Tuapse.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7714</p>
